---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { network, forms, routes, founding } from '../lib/network';
import { url } from '../lib/url';

const hasEmail = Boolean(network.contact_email);
---

<Base
  title={founding ? 'Join the founding cohort' : 'Join'}
  description="How a lab joins the network, how to follow the seminars, and how to nominate a speaker."
>
  <h1>{founding ? 'Join the founding cohort' : 'Join'}</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    {founding
      ? 'Labs across the Greater Bay Area are invited to establish a shared seminar and collaboration network. Membership is by lab, there are no fees, and the founding labs shape the rules.'
      : 'Membership is by lab. A PI submits one entry; a coordinator reviews it; the lab appears on the roster.'}
  </p>

  <div class="actions" style="margin-top:0">
    {hasEmail ? (
      <>
        <a class="btn primary" href={routes.joinEmail}>Join by email</a>
        <a class="btn" href={forms.lab}>Join via GitHub</a>
      </>
    ) : (
      <a class="btn primary" href={forms.lab}>Submit your lab</a>
    )}
    <a class="btn" href={routes.follow}>Follow the seminars</a>
  </div>
  {!hasEmail && (
    <p class="small muted">
      The form needs a free GitHub account. If that is a problem, ask any member PI to submit for you; an email route
      will appear here once the network's address is set up.
    </p>
  )}

  <h2>Who</h2>
  <dl class="facts">
    <dt>Member lab</dt>
    <dd>A PI-led group at an institution in the Greater Bay Area. Listed, hosts seminars in turn, invites speakers on behalf of all.</dd>
    <dt>Affiliate lab</dt>
    <dd>A lab elsewhere that takes part regularly. Listed with a badge.</dd>
    <dt>Students, postdocs, research staff and other participants</dt>
    <dd>
      No application. <a href={routes.follow}>Follow the seminars</a>
      {hasEmail ? (
        <> and <a href={routes.followEmail}>ask to join the announcement list</a>, which carries the meeting links.</>
      ) : (
        <>. The announcement list, which carries the meeting links, is passed on by any member PI.</>
      )}
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>How</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      {hasEmail ? (
        <>Send the <a href={routes.joinEmail}>pre-filled email</a>, or open the <a href={forms.lab}>GitHub form</a> if you prefer.</>
      ) : (
        <>Open the <a href={forms.lab}>lab form</a>.</>
      )}
    </li>
    <li>Name, institution, city, up to eight keywords, two sentences on the lab. A photo is optional; initials are shown otherwise.</li>
    <li>
      Give consent. The entry's text is published under CC BY 4.0. A photo, if given, is displayed with your permission
      only and is not licensed for reuse.
    </li>
    <li>A coordinator reviews the entry, usually within days, and the lab appears on the roster.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Also</h2>
  <dl class="facts">
    <dt><a href={routes.nominateEmail || forms.nomination}>Nominate a speaker</a></dt>
    <dd>
      Anyone may.
      {hasEmail ? (
        <> Nominations by email stay with the coordinators. The <a href={forms.nomination}>GitHub route</a> is public.</>
      ) : (
        <> Nominations are read by the coordinators and never published on the site; the form is a public GitHub issue, so write only what the nominee could read.</>
      )}
    </dd>
    <dt><a href={forms.event}>Propose an event</a></dt>
    <dd>Seminars, workshops, summer schools. See the <a href={url('docs/speaker-kit/')}>speaker kit</a> for the format.</dd>
    <dt><a href={forms.tutorial}>Share a tutorial</a></dt>
    <dd>Notebooks, courses, recordings. The material stays where you host it.</dd>
    <dt><a href={forms.position}>Post a position</a></dt>
    <dd>PhD, postdoc, RA, faculty. Listings expire on their deadline.</dd>
  </dl>

  <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
    To change or remove an entry, write to the coordinators or edit its file by pull request. The rules are in the{' '}
    <a href={url('docs/charter/')}>charter</a>, a draft for ratification by the founding labs, and the{' '}
    <a href={url('docs/privacy-and-consent/')}>privacy statement</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
